|>I'm looking for a utility or program that will convert documents
|>created using the VT100 graphics character set to a standard
|>Postscript file.  Does any kind soul out there know of one?
|>Thanks for your attention.
|>

DEC (assume you're on a DEC system :) provides filters for ansi-to-ps
printing. On VMS, they are build into the printing mechanism as
generic queues (printer_CPS_ANSI named queues), on ultrix there are
datatypes for this, i.e. you can do a lpr -Dansi

At least on ultrix it should be no problem to locate the filter
(likely in /usr/lib/lpdfilters) and missuse it for other-than-printing
purposes.

The one REAL problem here may be that only the DEC sold PS printers
contain the DECtech fonts to do the thing you want...

