There's only one approved general algorithm for translating published benchmark
ratings into meaningful numbers:

1) Multiply the published value by zero.

2) Add the value YOU get when running YOUR code.

That said, "officially" 1 VUP = 1 MIPS = 1 SPECmark; the benchmarks are all
scaled relative to an 11/780.  (MIPS is actually an absolute number, but
the 780 was very close to 1 MIPS for a "standard" instruction stream.)


