Except the topic of discussion if a MicroVAX II, not a MicroVAX 3800.

The simplest way to determine the ethernet address is to log onto
a node with 'bootnode="yes"', do a $REP/ENA, and type "B XQ" on the 
MicroVAX II. On the screen that you do a $REP/ENA, you will see 
the ethernet address of the MVII. It will also say something to the 
effect of 'boot failed' or something like that because you have not
yet created a boot file for this machine.

