> 
> command doesn't work on a microvax II (this is the first one I've had to 
> deal with).  The address does not seem to be printed on the board itself
> anywhere either (or is it?) 
> 
> Could someone please enlighten me with a procedure of finding said address
> out?

Try this:

>>> b/100 xq
 BOOTFILE: read_addr

I believe this requires that you have another VAX on your network to
process this request (i.e. you're asking another machine to read your
address for you).  This is documented in the Guide to Setting up a Vax
Cluster, maybe other places also.

Hope this helps.


