In article <231bl1$9u1@umd5.umd.edu>, bleau@umdsp.umd.edu writes:

> Try
>>>> b/800 xq
> This boots from the delqa (or deqna) interface and uses a special protocol.
> You'll be prompted for a filename.  Enter
>     read_addr
> This'll asked the responding VMS system to download the program read_addr,
> which will run on the mvII.  It'll display your Ethernet address.
> 

  I believe that should be 

>>> B/100 XQ

  This sets the hexadecimal value 100 in R5 and then boots via the DELQA. 
The effect of setting this value ( bit 8 ) is to tell VMB to solicit the
name of a secondary bootstrap file. The file READ_ADDR.SYS is such a file,
which prints out the ethernet address of the controller and halts the CPU.

