>
>I have a microvax II with a delqua card that I need to find the
>ethernet hardware address for (in order to boot it in to my cluster)
>
>It seems that the 
>
>>>> show ether
>
>command doesn't work on a microvax II (this is the first one I've had to 
>deal with).  The address does not seem to be printed on the board itself
>anywhere either (or is it?) 
>
>Could someone please enlighten me with a procedure of finding said address
>out?

From the gray wall (VAXcluster Manual, Appendix C):

	NCP> SET LOGGING MONITOR EVENT 0.*
	NCP> SET LOGGING MONITOR STATE ON
	$ REPLY /ENABLE=NETWORK

Type these commands on any node.  Boot your MicroVAX II with

	>>> B XQA0

You'll see the service request message complete with the Ethernet address
on your terminal with the logging enabled.

