Yes, well, there are a couple reasons why I said that method.
Primarily, it's because I didn't have the manual in front of me
so I couldn't remember the specific parameters. ;-)
Secondarily, I gave this description because it is a very easy
way to create a satellite node. All you need to do is enable OPCOM
in a window, run CLUSTER_CONFIG, answer all the questions until you
get to the hardware address question, boot the MicroVAX you need
to add to the 'cluster, and cut-n-paste the 08-00-2b-ab-cd-ef address.

Sure, it sounds convoluted, but no more so than the B/100 procedure.
Not only that, but when you cut-n-paste, you don't have a chance of
transposing any of the characters by writing them down wrong or 
reading them back wrong. It's the same CLUSTER_CONFIG, the same
OPCOM (you should be paying attention to OPCOM when booting over
the 'net anyway so you can determine if everything is working or not),
and the same ethernet address except you don't have to write it down.


Chris
