LA210 dip switch settings
=========================

There are two banks. The one on the left is `A', the one on the right is `B'.

* indicates the factory default

A1 UP     Use speed control signals. (SPDI-12/SPDS-23)
   DOWN * Use transmission restraint via BUSY. (11)

A2 UP     Modem control.
   DOWN * No modem control.

A3 UP   A4 UP     Do not connect on fault.
   UP      DOWN   Send BREAK on fault.
   DOWN    UP     Disconnect (drop DTR) on fault.
   DOWN    DOWN * No action on fault.  (XOFF will be sent if enabled.)

A5 UP     Disconnect on reciept of EOT.
A5 DOWN * Ignore EOT.

A6 UP   * Enable XON/XOFF flow control.
   DOWN   Disable XON/XOFF flow control.

A7 UP     Print bad characters as recived on receiver error.
   DOWN * Print bad characters as SUB character on receiver error.

A8 SPECIAL: Store features switch

   Stores computer-selectable features in NVM. First send escape sequences
   to select desired features, then move A8 from DOWN to UP. Moving A8 from
   UP to DOWN has no effect. You can print a status test to verify settings.

B1-B5  Baud Rate Selection:

    50    DOWN DOWN DOWN DOWN DOWN 
    75    UP   DOWN DOWN DOWN DOWN 
   110    DOWN UP   DOWN DOWN DOWN 
   134.5  UP   UP   DOWN DOWN DOWN 
   150    DOWN DOWN UP   DOWN DOWN 
   200    UP   DOWN UP   DOWN DOWN 
   300    DOWN UP   UP   DOWN DOWN 
   600    UP   UP   UP   DOWN DOWN 
  1200    DOWN DOWN DOWN UP   DOWN 
  1800    UP   DOWN DOWN UP   DOWN 
  2400    DOWN UP   DOWN UP   DOWN 
  4800 *  UP   UP   DOWN UP   DOWN 
  7200    DOWN DOWN UP   UP   DOWN 
  9600    UP   DOWN UP   UP   DOWN 

 75/ 600  DOWN DOWN DOWN DOWN UP   
 75/1200  UP   DOWN DOWN DOWN UP   
150/ 600  DOWN UP   DOWN DOWN UP   
150/1200  UP   UP   DOWN DOWN UP   
300/2400  DOWN DOWN UP   DOWN UP   
300/4800  UP   DOWN UP   DOWN UP   
600/2400  DOWN UP   UP   DOWN UP   
600/4800  UP   UP   UP   DOWN UP   

B6 UP   B7 UP     ODD Parity
   UP      DOWN   MARK Parity   (8-bit NO Parity)
   DOWN    UP     EVEN Parity
   DOWN    DOWN * SPACE Parity  (8-bit NO Parity)

B8 UP   * 8-bit data format
   DOWN   7-bit data format

