My group manages a cluster of (mostly) 6000-series VAXes with an
ever-increasing satellite DECnet network of VS4000's. The VS4000's aren't
clustered, and reside in several remotely-located buildings to act as
PATHworks servers. We've been using TLZ06 4mm tape drives local to these
stations for backups that run unattended at night, and it's worked well so
far. But, even with a compacted 90 meter tape, it's inevitable that the
capacity of the latest RZ disks will exceed the capacity of a single tape,
and we're rapidly loading the SCSI buses on these stations full of 'em.
Since we don't have an operator that can respond to a request for a second
tape for these backups, I'm sitting on a problem waiting to happen. 

