Comparing power cords etc from USA to Europe is more then
hazardus!

One never knows (if one does not look in the apropriate drawing)
how things are connected. Besides, it is a habit to manufactre
the equipment in several versions, especially regarding power
and voltage.

It might be that equipment is connected "1-phase" on one version 
(live to neutral), and "3-phase" in anoter version (live to live, 
ie one phase to anoter). This might be the case, for example, 
some engine needs 220 V across the coil. You could sell the same
equipment, if you give instructions to connect it "1-phase"
at places with 380V system (220/380, that is), and "2-phase"
at places with 220V system (127/220).

It is also posible you select to sell the equipment with another
engine in anoter country. 3-phase engines are usually cheaper
and simpler, but if nessesary, it could be operated from 1-phase
supply, using an extarnal capacitor.

All figures are to be taken with care. Several different systems 
exist, for instance 110/208, 127/220, 220/380, 230/400, ...

This whole case isn't exactly a scinece of it own, but it is on
the other hand mutch more than "just plug it in". In my private
opinion, several "system managers" might be VERY skilled at operating
the computers, once they are installd. That part, on the other hande
should be left to somebody skilled in installing.

Best regards /G|ran AA



