I am using DEC GKS3D v1.1 on a DECstation 5000/200PX under Ultrix 4.1
and have run into the following problem:

When I call the 'Request Locator' function [greqloc() in the
C-binding] within the following routine,  I get a cursor whose color
(black) happens to be indistinguishable from most of the background.

How can I force the cursor to take on a different color so that it can
be more easily seen?  I can find nothing in the DEC GKS3D documents
that sheds any light on this.

Thanks

- Grant



get_mouse_input(u,v)
     float *u,*v ;
{

  Gqloc response ;

  gsetlocmode(WSID,1,GREQUEST,GECHO) ;
  greqloc(WSID,1,&response) ;
  if (response.status == GNONE) {
    *u = 0.0 ;
    *v = 0.0 ;
    return(FALSE) ;
  }
  *u = response.loc.position.x ;
  *v = response.loc.position.y ;
  return(TRUE) ;
}
      



