In article <1993Jul23.150407.1@reddwf.enet.dec.com>, quodling@reddwf.enet.dec.com writes:
> TU60;s, TU58's, TU80's what about the TS03? What takeup spool? Actually, many
> of these were buyouts. But one thing I found back in those days, (when I was a
> Digital FS Engineer), was that a tape drive, properly tuned and cared for, ran
> like a dream. Problem was, most people didn't know how to, or were scared of
> doing the alignments etc...

  Indeed. We have 3 TU78's and a TU77 in constant use, and we've been very
happy with them. Of course, we do all of our own maintenance. I remember one
time when my FS rep wanted to run the TU78 data reliability test as part of a
PM. I went to get a short (150') tape, as this test writes all the way to the
end of the tape, reads it back, etc. The FS rep said "don't worry - it'll
bomb out in a few minutes". I gave him a 3600' tape and he got to watch it
for > 3 hours 8-}

  About the only *really* lame tape was the TS11. Of course, it was designed
as an "economy" drive, and it showed. A Japanese company named Anritsu de-
cided to clone it as their first entry into the DEC marketplace. *BIG* mis-
take...

  The TK50 is interesting. It shares a lot of design philosophy with the TS11
(put the smarts in the controller, talk to the drive over a serial bus). DEC
learned from the TS11. The user interface on the TK50 is pretty lame, though.
However, the prototype was even worse - just the red button and light - no
green LED on the left side. No way to tell if the drive was doing anything.
We had the first TK50 in this FS region (many years ago) and got the tape
wedged in the drive in the first half hour. We called DEC FS and the rep came
out, looked at it, and refused to work on it, saying "this can't be made by
DEC (despite the label) - it's to much of a piece of <junk>!".

  The TZ30 is a really nice drive, however. It's everything the TK50 should
have been. I believe it's built for DEC (as opposed to *by* DEC), from some
vendor in Japan. And the current drives (TF/TZ/TA8xx) are pretty nice, too.

