  You could get an account with DEC's Electronic Store, which will let you
look up part numbers, determine prices, look at marketing descriptions, etc.
They're on Tymnet as "dec.demo". There's an 800 number as well, but I don't
recall what it is. You could call 800-DIGITAL (this gets you a human, not
a computer) and ask for the Store's number.

  At the next level, there's the Digital Assisted Services catalog. This
lists all of the parts DEC is prepared to sell you without a fuss, as well
as repair prices, documentation, diagnostics, etc. Call 800-225-5385 to ask
for a copy.

  Next level is the product microfiche library for your area(s) of interest -
PDP-11, VAX, Alpha, PC. This costs money (a few thousand dollars a year for
the complete set).

  Next is the Option Module Summary. You have to be a DEC employee to get
one [legitimately]. It's over a thousand pages of part numbers and descrip-
tions. It is rumored to come out quarterly, and some used equipment dealers
might have old copies. It's unlikely they'd admit to it, though. Anyway, most
of what you need to know can be found on the Store or in the DAS catalog.

