In article <22gm6r$9em@taloa.unice.fr> desnogue@mimosa.unice.fr writes:
}I am using `as' version 2.1 under Ultrix to assemble code
}output by a code generator I'm writing.

}   - In Kane & Heinrich 's book pp D-19ff., the $fp register
}     is mentionned (under the name virtual frame pointer);
}     does this register really exist (for the compiler kit I
}     mean) or is it really `virtual' ?
}     Anyway which register should I use for $fp ? I'm currently
}     using $30 (s8).

   According to D-20 and D-21 the general use is:

       subu   $sp,framesize
       .frame $sp,framesize,$31

   That is to say, there is no real reason to save the previous
   version of $sp in some register as ``$fp'' -- you can get at
   whatever you want with offsets from $sp.  So it really is
   virtual (I'm not sure why they even mentioned it, actually).

John
