Try writing out, say, Maxwell's equations for the electromagnetic field, in
plain everyday English, and you'll begin to understand what jargon is really
for.  It is not real English, but it *is* real language, and just as valid as
any other language.  Where we get into trouble is in using specialized language
in conversing with nonspecialists -- just as we do in shouting English at those
who speak only, say, French.

Once you've polished off Maxwell, you can try translating a *complete* model of
QCD into Basic English.  Good luck....
