Oh, I thought you were talking about _grammatical_ constructions
(which might be--see Chomsky).  Pronounceable words?  Maybe...but I'm
not sure this is true with any narrow definition of "pronounceable."
I've met a lot of people (non-native speakers of the respective
languages, of course) who simply could not master nasalized and
umlauted vowels, despite the fact that these are easy for native
French or German speakers.  And I can't even make a respectable
attempt at a glottal click.

> and they all want computers to do things for them.  Mark my words, if
