>#talking about how YOU interact with YOURSELF.  I'm not about to type
>#"compile program john.text" instead of "cc j.c" just because somebody
>#else in the world doesn't understand it.
>
Here I have to take the side of music.  The fact is that, although
what you type on the command line is your business, what you put in a
file (or what others must type on a command line to access your file)
may not be.  I, for one (although many might disagree with me) would
much rather debug someone else's Pascal code than someone else's C
code.  Readability by the public _is_ an issue.




