You might try specifying 'b 512' on the Ultrix system (SGI tar defaults
to 512 or 256KB blocks with DAT).  If that still doesn't do it, you
might try writing the tape with a smaller blocking factor explictly,
although this seems to have been primarily a problem with Sun (and some
HP releases), and not with Ultrix.

Seems many versions of tar won't correctly figure out the block size
if it is 'large'.
