In <22287bINN65r@gap.caltech.edu> mvanier@smaug.cns.caltech.edu (Michael Vanier) writes:

>I've been having trouble running xterm on a DEC alpha.  It seems that
>the EOF character control-D doesn't work.  Is there a way around this?

I had the same problem with tcsh. control-D was mapped to WERASE *and* EOF.
Trying to change WEARSE with stty didn't work.
The mapping is correct if you have a look in termios.h (OSF_SOURCE defined).
I didn't like it either so I recompiled tcsh with a little modified termios.h
(WERASE mapped to control-W). No problems so far.

/Henk
