  8-plane VCB02's can be had here in the US for about US $250 for the 3-board
set and cabinet kit. They definitely work with the KA65x CPU's. They use the
same monitors as the VCB01, but can also do color. Mono monitors are any of
the DEC 1024 x 864 models (VR260, VR262, VR150, etc) and color monitors would
be any of the color 1204 x 864 units (like the VR290). Things like the VR319
(mono) and the VRT19 (color) won't work as they're designed for 1280 x 1024
only. Actually, the VRT19 might work as it's really a Sony multiple-scan-rate
monitor, but I haven't tried it.

  Be careful with the VCB02 and cables - there are different cabinet kits and
external cables for mono and color. If at all possible, buy the color versions
and use the green cable to run a mono monitor - that way you can upgrade later
without tearing the system apart.

