sspatter@netcom.com (Spatters) writes:

>Hi.

>     How do I access above 64K on my PDP-11/34a from the octal console?
>I am trying to write a little mini-os for my machine but I can't figure
>out how to get beyond 177,777 Octal.  I'm fine with that being a code-
>length max, but I'd like to access the rest of the RAM on the machine,
>for data and caching of drives and such.  Any thoughts, help, advice,
>or whatnot would be greatly appreciated.

The architecture of the pdp-11 allows a maximum of 64kb to be directly
accessible at any one time.  If you wish to access memory beyond that,
you'll have to enable memory relocation and make use of the mapping
registers to map different parts of the PHYSICAL address space into
your 64kb VIRTUAL address space.

					Megan Gentry
					ex-Member RT-11 Development Team

