   I'll bet we make this an addition to the FAQ soon:

   Pin     Signal
    1      Data Terminal Ready (DTR)
    2      Transmit Data
    3      Ground (Ref to Xmt Data)
    4      Ground (Ref to Rcv Data)
    5      Receive Data
    6      Data Set Ready (DSR)

   Do you see a pattern here? A loopback connector that DEC has is connected:
   1<>6, 2<>5, and 3<>4. The signals are said to be DEC423 which might be
   thought of as RS-423 and possibly an out-growth of RS-232-x.

