 thewalt@canuck.CE.Berkeley.EDU (Christopher Robin Thewalt) writes:
>                              Also, the brain dead getty raises and
> lowers DTR while waiting for an incoming call, and the modem won't
> answer when DTR is down, so you'll need DTR overide in the modem too.

It could be a brain-dead modem asserting DSR when it's not off hook.
Most modem have settings that will allow following the EIA-232 standard,
which controls DSR from the modem, and its response to DTR (it should
hang up the line when DTR is dropped).  Unfortunately, most modems by
default don't follow the standard, so you have to tell them to behave.

If getty raises and lowers DTR because DSR is asserted, then it's doing
the "right thing".
