the Courier has the following settings for DSR (&Sn):

	&S0	DSR is always ON (override).  Default
	&S1	in originate mode, the modem sends DSR after it dials,
		when it detects the remote modem's answer tone.  in
		answer mode, the modem sends DSR after it sends an
		answer tone.
	&S2	this option is for specialized equipment such as
		automatic callback units.  On loss of carrier, the
		modem sends a pulsed DSR signal with CTS following CD.
	&S3	this is the same as &S2, but without CTS following CD.

are you saying that the default is wrong?  one should use &S1?  could
