nina@fynu.ucl.ac.be (Alain Ninane - FYNU) writes:

>Folks,
>I'm installing my new DSP5350 disk on a DECStation and I'm wondering
>whether the jumper 21-22 on the option connector should be connected
>or not.  The installation guide says that this jumper is used to enable
>the spindle synchronization ... What does that mean ?

Spindle synchronization is useful, if you want to use such an disk
in an array configuration, e.g. in a RAID or so. You could then 
connect all disks in a set with an extra cable, and your disk will
spin synchronously, all with the same sector under their heads.

On normal uses (e.g. on your DECstation), you should not enable
spindle synchronization. Your disk could eventually fail to spin,
if its enabled, and no sync cable is connected, or spin without
a constant speed.

Sincerely,
Klaus
