In article <1993Jul2.162928.22747@news.cs.indiana.edu> "Bill Wang" <wcwang@cs.indiana.edu> writes:
>I have noticed the same problem on OSF.  It seems to be the case that
>'keypad.el' and 'vt???.el' are not loaded into e-lisp space when
>emacs is running from a terminal.  Any help would be appreciated.

When emacs is using its own X window, it is reading keyboard events not
escape sequences like it would running in an xterm window.  You'd have to
modify emacs to generate escape sequences for the keypad keys since it
does not check for them; it only checks for function keys.  See 
the emacs source file src/x11term.c for details.


