Well, my email to you bounced after 72 hrs of attempts to deliever.

A few things to look into.

1) Make sure the plotter is in X-on/X-off mode.  Some of the older HP
Plotters come up in HP ACQ/ENQ mode.    You can usually change the 
handshaking method by careful programming before sending any plotter
data.

2) If they don't come up either ACQ/ENQ or X-on/X-off mode, they are 
probably looking for a hardware handshake instead.  You should check 
you machine documentation to see if the port you are using supports
them.

